Root cause:
The bug was caused by the use of an incorrect class reference for `RangeInputSplit` in the `AccumuloInputFormat` and `EmptySplitsAccumuloInputFormat` classes. The code was referencing the deprecated `org.apache.accumulo.core.client.mapred.RangeInputSplit` instead of the correct `org.apache.accumulo.core.client.mapreduce.RangeInputSplit`. This led to potential issues in handling input splits correctly, as the deprecated class may not have the expected behavior or properties needed for the current implementation. The patch corrects these references to ensure the proper class is used, thereby fixing the bug.
